findings.body:
`build_scope` receives both lists in one positional array. It runs `shift 11`, takes `only_count` values as pathspecs (executable_revmux-round.sh:89-93), and treats everything left over as exclusions. `next` builds `scope_args` with pathspecs first, then exclusions (lines 376-383). Test 016 uses `--exclude` without `--only`. Tests 026-028 use `--only` without `--exclude`. Test 026's awk filter also drops the `Exclusions:` section before asserting.

The goal requires `--only` and `--exclude` to stay separate, and requires the tests to fail if that regresses. Several regressions would leave every test green:
- swapping the append order;
- miscounting the shift;
- copying the only values without shifting them off (`${@:1:only_count}`).

Any of these would put exclusion text into `Limited to:` and into the read commands, or list the `--only` paths under `Exclusions:`. Scale, Commits and Changed files would still look correct, because `next` computes them directly from `only_values`.

The bar's PDF action calls the same `download()` and checks the same `canGenerate` as the card's button. Only the card renders the reason the action is blocked or in progress:
- the label switches to 'Подготовка PDF…' while busy (line ~868);
- a status paragraph shows 'Создаём PDF…' or 'Обрабатываем изображения…';
- `draftError` is shown there too.

The bar exists for the case where the card is scrolled out of view, so none of that feedback is on screen when the bar is in use. The bar's button has a fixed `aria-label="Скачать PDF"`.

Concrete case: the user scrolls down to the minis list and clicks 'Скачать PDF' in the bar. The button just goes grey (fieldset `disabled={busy}`) for the whole PDF generation, with no visible or announced progress. Likewise, if the button is disabled while images are still being prepared, or because of an uncommitted invalid margin draft, the bar shows a dead button with no reason. The card's button announces both states.
